From 8a9b80e9a66f9fecb88f31af70a06b82da33f01c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:56:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): ribbon pins go through an undoable SetRibbonPins
 command

Pinning a ribbon cell wrote the RibbonPins singleton straight from the
pane (panes.rs toggle_pin -> ribbon::pinned_set). Pins are saved with
the project, so that was a document change the history never saw: it
could not be undone and could not mark the document unsaved, against
AGENTS.md's "Everything Is a Command".

A new app command, SetRibbonPins, records the previous and next list
(cleaned like pinned_set) and refuses a no-op; toggle_pin executes it
on the history. Undo/redo now walk pins like any other change, and
once the history tracks unsaved state (#107, PR #141) a pin marks the
document dirty with no further change. The M6.2 "pins are layout, not
a command" comments are updated to say so.

Fixes #143

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
